      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Update: While initially I thought I had found the culprit, it seems that was a bit of a red herring. \n\nAfter going through every script causing issues and making sure execution orders were correct, the issue is still present. Did the classic \"spread Debug.Log everywhere\" method and what I've found is that despite using the [DefaultExecutionOrder()] attribute on ALL affected classes, the p-test build is not respecting these values whatsoever. Build+testing the exact same build on p-test and the live client results in very different execution orders.\n\nI don't have more info than that currently, as I've been too busy IRL recently to test further. But I do believe there is a deeper problem with execution orders in p-test.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
